{
  "version": 2,
  "comparator": "AGENTS.md: Jet beats every peer on every metric. A cell is one workload, one Jet tier (jet-bin: the `jet build --release` binary; jet-run: `jet run run.jet`, warm) and one peer, for one metric (wall, cpu, rss); its ratio is Jet over the peer. A ratio of 1.00 or more is a LOSS. Peers are never averaged; every peer counts. A peer that prints the wrong output or overruns the timeout is an error, not a win.",
  "method": {
    "rounds": 3,
    "warmup": 2,
    "runs": 5,
    "slow_ms": 10000,
    "slow_warmup": 0,
    "slow_runs": 1,
    "timeout_s": 120,
    "note": "hyperfine -N with every command of a workload in one invocation per round; the command order rotates by one each round, so the commands interleave. Wall is the median of all timed runs, CPU the mean of user + system, RSS the largest peak across runs. A command whose correctness run takes over slow_ms gets slow_warmup and slow_runs per round (the correctness run itself warms the caches)."
  },
